Intake:
1. Use the previous successful heartbeat as the intake start; first run uses the preceding three hours. Pin every issue created or reopened in the window, including unlabeled issues.
2. For each intake issue, read the complete live body/comments, linked issues/PRs, labels, implementation state, and repository evidence. Validate directive fidelity, bounded scope, runtime control point, ACs/proof, ICL, priority, branch slug, lane, and workflow status.
3. Attribute the underlying source using timestamps, wording, MoP events, read-only slot logs, admission logs, and /tmp artifacts. Report PM, slot 1/2/3/4, CTO/Codex, customer/production alert, automation, or unknown with concrete evidence; never infer from the shared GitHub actor alone.
4. Route immediately: clean bounded app-code/app-test -> repair contract and status:todo; live dependency -> status:backlog + pm-blocked:dependency with canonical blockers/wake; tracking/investigation/repro/external/infra/direct-main/deferred/CTO -> canonical non-Todo disposition with reason, owner, next action, wake, evidence. Keep internal control-plane work out of Todo. Close only conclusively duplicate/completed work with unambiguous evidence; otherwise report a proposed closure.

Mandatory repository-wide untriaged/status-hygiene sweep:
U1. On every run, query every open GitHub issue, not only the intake window or current Ready Pool surface. Pin every issue with zero or more than one `status:*` label into the run snapshot.
U2. For each such issue, read the complete live body/comments, linked issues/PRs, labels, implementation state, and repository evidence. Assign exactly one canonical status and repair its labels and body metadata directly: clean bounded app-code/app-test -> status:todo after full dispatch-contract/ICL/proof repair; live dependency -> status:backlog + pm-blocked:dependency with exact blockers and wake; low-priority explicitly parked work -> status:deferred; active execution/review/QA -> its single live lifecycle status; tracking/investigation/external/infra/direct-main/product/CTO -> canonical non-Todo status/disposition with owner, next action, wake, and evidence.
U3. Resolve conflicting status labels. Close only conclusively completed, duplicate, or superseded work with unambiguous live evidence; otherwise keep it open in exactly one canonical status.
U4. The run cannot finish while any open issue has zero or multiple `status:*` labels. Treat every mutation failure as ACTION REQUIRED and report the exact issue number.

Pinned snapshot and audit:
5. Pin one snapshot containing every open status:todo issue, every open pm-blocked:dependency issue, every intake issue, every open issue with zero or multiple `status:*` labels, and every full-surface backlog promotion candidate. Do not rebuild or substitute the snapshot during the run.
6. Run pm-operator backlog-report but treat it as a detector rather than the source of truth. Read complete live state for every pinned issue you may mutate.

Mandatory Ready Pool repair loop:
7. Audit every pinned Todo exactly once. Every Todo must have exactly one status, exactly one canonical P0/P1/P2/P3 label, a valid Issue Contract Ledger, and complete Ready Pool metadata: priority, lane, bounded ac_summary, claimable_slot_type, blockers, work_type, branch_slug, required_validation, owner, next_action, wake_condition, and disposition. Repair every missing, stale, or contradictory field directly in the issue body and labels during this run.
8. Keep only bounded app-code or app-test work claimable by dev slots in status:todo. Move docs-only, internal control-plane, infra/direct-main, tracking, investigation/repro, deferred, and unresolved CTO/product work out of Todo into its canonical lane with a structured reason, owner, next action, wake condition, evidence, and fingerprint. A Todo with live blockers is a defect: move it to dependency wait or repair stale blockers.
9. Canonical priority rules: verified active critical incident P0; bugs and user-visible lag P1; PRM, benchmarking, and agency/workspace features P2; genuinely low-priority bounded work P3. Body metadata and label must match exactly.

Mandatory dependency-graph repair loop:
10. Audit every pinned pm-blocked:dependency issue, not just issues surfaced as promoter candidates. Parse the canonical blockers from Ready Pool metadata, verify each referenced issue and PR live, and reconstruct each dependency chain or DAG from the pinned snapshot.
11. For every chain, identify its current executable head: an open bounded app-code/app-test node whose real predecessors are all closed/merged and whose required proof gates are satisfied. Promote every such head immediately to status:todo, remove status:backlog and pm-blocked:dependency, set blockers:none, rewrite disposition to PROMOTE, preserve or repair its canonical priority/ICL/branch slug/validation contract, and validate dispatch readiness. Ten Todos is a minimum, never a maximum.
12. If a mechanically closed blocker was split, superseded, or replaced by open children, rewrite blockers to the live successor(s) and keep DEPENDENCY_WAIT; never promote from closure alone. If a parent/tracker has claimable children, keep the tracker nonclaimable and promote the earliest dependency-free child. Canonical blocker metadata wins over incidental prose, but repair the prose so both agree.
13. No chain may finish the run with an eligible head still in backlog, a closed/nonexistent stale blocker, a Todo carrying dependency labels, or a downstream child promoted ahead of an open predecessor. Continue repairing until those invariants hold.

Backlog promotion and final validation:
14. Promote every other clean bounded dependency-free app-code/app-test backlog candidate. Do not promote tracking, external, investigation/repro, deferred, docs-only, infra/direct-main, or unresolved CTO/product work.
15. After mutations, validate every changed body with the canonical ICL validator, run focused Ready Pool/dependency checks for all changed issues, then rerun the full dry-run audit. Finish only when all Todos are dispatch-valid, all intake is classified, every open issue has exactly one canonical `status:*` label, no eligible dependency head remains in backlog, no stale dependency metadata remains, and status_hygiene/backlog_promote_candidate/todo contract defect buckets are zero. Report exact mutation failures; never silently skip or stop at diagnosis.

