Re-read the live issue lifecycle after ancestry/validation checks. Merged ancestry or deployed validation is readiness evidence, never a close command. A later deliberate reopen is authoritative: an OPEN issue with status:todo, status:in-progress, or status:in-review plus an explicit customer-verification artifact, template, or reporter wake must remain OPEN with labels preserved. Close only with explicit terminal-close intent, a verified customer-verification terminal, or the existing unambiguous duplicate/completion proof. Missing, stale, or contradictory lifecycle/wake evidence fails closed and remains open with one owner, next action, and wake. Never replace protected nonterminal state with status:done.
